SUMMARY:Improvised Shakespeare 101 With Renee!
DESCRIPTION:Discover how to improvise in Shakespeare’s style in this adva
 nced improv class. About the Class: Love. Jealousy. Betrayal. Ambition. Sh
 akespeare used powerful emotions to tell timeless stories that still capti
 vate audiences today–and you can too! Learn the building blocks of impro
 vised Shakespeare including language patterns\, narrative devices\, and ch
 aracter archetypes to create a larger-than-life Shakespearean comedy on th
 e spot. This class will add techniques to your improv toolkit to use in im
 provised Shakespeare and beyond. This class requires students to have comp
 leted LIP's Improv 201 or Artistic Director approval. Students must be 18 
 or older for this class. This Class will run Wednesdays from 7pm-9:30pm on
  the following dates: 10/7\, 10/14\, 10/21\, 10/28\, 11/4\, 11/11\, 11/18\
 , [no class 11/25]\, and 12/2. This class has a class show on Thursday 12/
 3 at 7:00pm! Ticket sale close at the end of the day on Sunday 10/4/26. Im
 portant: Please check your email the week prior to the start date of your 
 class for any updates. To qualify for the class show you must: Adhere to t
 he Lancaster Improv Players' Code of Conduct. Attend at least six of the e
 ight sessions (ideally all eight). Tickets are on sale until end of day Su
